{"text": "Garside Wilmot LLP — ATTENDANCE NOTE\nClient: Mrs Winifred Mary Arkwright · Matter: ARK/0412/LPA · Fee earner: Honor\nWilmot (HW) · Date: 11 November 2025 · Time: 1 hr 20 mins · Home visit\n\nAttendance\nHW attending Mrs Arkwright at her home, The Old Forge, 9 Church Lane, Pateley\nBridge, Harrogate HG3 5LB. Her son Julian Arkwright let me in and then, at my\nrequest, left for the whole of the meeting.\n\nMrs Arkwright is 92 (born 3 April 1933). She was a schoolteacher and is very clear\nabout what she wants. She is registered partially sighted, so I read each section of\nForm LP1F aloud. She told me her GP said in the summer that she has mild\ncognitive impairment; she scored 26 out of 30 on the MMSE in August. I asked the\nusual open questions under the Mental Capacity Act 2005. She explained in her\nown words what an attorney can and cannot do, and why she does not want the\nbank \"deciding for her.\" I have no concerns about capacity or pressure.\n\nInstructions\n Both types of LPA: property and financial affairs, and health and welfare.\n Attorneys: Julian (son, born 19.07.1961, of 14 Ripon Road, Harrogate HG1 2JB)\nand her granddaughter Tamsin Pargeter (born 2 Feb 1992, of Flat 2, 61 Otley\nRoad, Leeds LS6 3AB), to act jointly and severally.\n She does NOT want her younger son to be notified. She said only that he \"has\nhad his troubles with money and with drink\" and has not visited since 2021.\n Life-sustaining treatment: attorneys to decide. She is a Quaker and wants a\nsimple funeral at the meeting house; noted, though not for the LPA itself.\n Certificate provider: her GP, Dr Rohan Seneviratne, who has known her for\neleven years. Dr Seneviratne will call on Friday 14th.\n\nAssets (for the Will Trust file as well)\n The house, unencumbered, about £465,000. Title number NYK204418.\n Nidderdale Building Society instant access account: sort code 60-83-71, account\n44187209, about £38,600.\n Premium Bonds, holder's number 104418772: £50,000.\n Teachers' pension, £1,412.50 a month; state pension. NI number ZT 41 87 20 B.\n Life interest under The Arkwright Will Trust (her late husband's will, 1998):\none half of the house is held in the trust.\n\nCosts and next steps\nFixed fee £850 plus VAT for both LPAs, plus the Office of the Public Guardian\nregistration fees of £82 each. She does not qualify for a fee remission. She paid\n£200 on account by cheque no. 000318.\n\nEngrossments to be posted, large print. Any queries: she prefers the landline,\n01632 960188, after 10am. Julian's mobile 07700 900131; Tamsin's email\ntamsin.pargeter@ridingsmail.example.", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 445 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Winifred Mary Arkwright", "Julian Arkwright", "Tamsin Pargeter", "Rohan Seneviratne", "Julian", "Tamsin"], "companies": ["Garside Wilmot LLP", "Nidderdale Building Society", "Office of the Public Guardian", "ridingsmail", "Example"]}, "topics": {"places": ["The Old Forge", "9 Church Lane", "Pateley Bridge", "Harrogate", "14 Ripon Road", "Flat 2", "61 Otley Road", "Leeds", "NYK204418"], "health": ["mild cognitive impairment", "MMSE", "none"], "sensitive": ["Quaker"], "names": ["Winifred Mary", "Julian", "Tamsin", "Rohan"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 75.89999999850988, "modelMs": 20499, "topicMs": 27578.5, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "Garside Wilmot LLP", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Garside Wilmot LLP"}, {"start": 49, "end": 72, "text": "Winifred Mary Arkwright", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Winifred Mary Arkwright"}, {"start": 83, "end": 95, "text": "ARK/0412/LPA", "k